A||N||5||fastback87||Dry Nitrous Kit Question???||||5||
Z||000000||fastback87||11-01-2001||01:57 PM||||I am new to nitrous and just bought a "dry kit" I have read many different opinions on which is better wet or dry.  I think I understand that for less than 150hp boost, the dry is the better kit.  More than 150hp you need to go with the wet kit.  Now I want the experts on pennock's to let me know what the facts are.  Just the facts please, as I have heard almost all of the opinions.<P>thanks a lot, <BR>James||||reg||5
Z||000001||Fiero_24||11-01-2001||03:21 PM||||I am looking for less than 100HP gain from Nitrous, but I am going with the Wet kit.  I have talked with a lot of people on what to do, and this is just the way I am going to go.<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/driverside41.jpg"> <BR>  <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fiero_24" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/fiero_24</A> <BR>1987 GT||||reg||14
Z||000002||Turbo88||11-01-2001||03:34 PM||||The difference is that a "dry" kit relies on the existing fuel system to add the extra fuel needed to prevent a lean condition. A wet kit adds it's own extra fuel so the stock system doesn't have to worry about it. Dry kits are much easier to install and are recommended for lower power levels. Wet kits are more complicated but require less or no work to your exisiting fuel system. As far as what the power level is on a 2.8? No idea <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">. I know that most people running an LT1 or LS1 like to use wet kits beyond 150hp. ||||reg||1
Z||000003||MinnGreenGT||11-01-2001||03:55 PM||||Fastback... you're not having 2nd thoughts about the kit you just bought are you?   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">  All the info above is pretty much correct.  You will do just fine with the Dry kit a the lower HP level... 1FST2M6 is using a Wet kit, and his results show how effective it is.  Good luck with your NOS!||||reg||1
Z||000004||Turbo88||11-01-2001||04:43 PM||||Yeah but 1FST2M6 sniffs his juice !! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> J/K. ||||reg||1
Z||000005||sluppy123||11-01-2001||04:57 PM||||Having had a Dry NOS kit on my GT, I'd say spend a little more $$ and get the Wet kit 1FST2M6 is running. Wet kits are less likely to run the engine lean, and you can run a bigger shot of N2O.<P>Just my .02<BR><P>------------------<BR>-Brian, Toolmaker<BR>Lincoln, NE<BR>87' GT-Galaxy silver mettalic, Turbo Charged, Modified 2.8- 235 HP w/ 7 psi Boost, Eibach Sport springs, RSM side scoops, Mr Mikes leather, 17" Mille Miglia's. <BR>                <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1711832&a=12781563&p=54316496&Sequence=0"> ||||reg||1
